Subject: [PATCH] arena: copper, tin and iron rocks on Entrana for the
 four-goal control test

Six natural rock locs (shape 10, angle 0) appended to the level-0 LOC section
of m44_52: copperrock1 2860,3348; tinrock1 2854,3337; ironrock1 2852,3340;
copperrock2 2860,3351; tinrock2 2862,3351; ironrock2 2851,3338.

Rule (runescape repo baseline/config.py START_SETS arena): from the start
2859,3342 and its seven seeded jitter tiles, candidate tiles are 6-16
walking steps from the start (baked SDK collision, doors open), have no loc
of their own, have eight walkable neighbours with no npc or obj spawn, and
lie within 32 tiles of every start. Candidates are taken in order of
(steps, x, z), at least 2 tiles apart, and each is kept only if blocking it
changes no walking distance from any start to the nearest tree, oak, net
spot and chicken and cuts off no reachable tile within 60. Types alternate
copper, tin, iron in pick order.
